 "text": "City of Alexander - McKenzie County, ND\nYou are using an outdated browser. Please upgrade your browser to improve your experience.\nSkip to content\nSkip to navigation\nSite map\nOfficial government website\nQuick top menu links Jobs\nEvents\nAction toolbar\nAnswers\nPayments\nReport Issue\nTranslate\nTranslate language select\nSelect language Afrikaans Albanian Amharic Arabic Armenian Azerbaijani Basque Belarusian Bengali Bosnian Bulgarian Catalan Cebuano Chichewa Chinese (Simplified) Chinese (Traditional) Corsican Croatian Czech Danish Dutch English Esperanto Estonian Filipino Finnish French Frisian Galician Georgian German Greek Gujarati Haitian Creole Hausa Hawaiian Hebrew Hindi Hmong Hungarian Icelandic Igbo Indonesian Irish Italian Japanese Javanese Kannada Kazakh Khmer Korean Kurdish (Kurmanji) Kyrgyz Lao Latin Latvian Lithuanian Luxembourgish Macedonian Malagasy Malay Malayalam Maltese Maori Marathi Mongolian Myanmar (Burmese) Nepali Norwegian Pashto Persian Polish Portuguese Punjabi Romanian Russian Samoan Scottish Gaelic Serbian Sesotho Shona Sindhi Sinhala Slovak Slovenian Somali Spanish Sundanese Swahili Swedish Tajik Tamil Telugu Thai Turkish Ukrainian Urdu Uzbek Vietnamese Welsh Xhosa Yiddish Yoruba Zulu\nSearch\nMcKenzie County, ND\nMenu\nPrimary menu links\nCommunity\nDepartments\nBoards\nServices\nNews\nContact\nMcKenzie County, ND\nCity of Alexander\nAbout\nCity Ordinances\nForms & Permits\nBoard and Councils\nCity of Alexander - Zoning District Map\nHome Rule Charter\nOld Settler’s Day\nBack\nAlexander City Council\nAlexander Zoning Board\nAlexander Park Board\nContact\nCity of Alexander\n(701) 828-3461\n(701) 828-3460 (FAX)\ncityofalexander@ruggedwest.com\nAlexander City Hall\n112 Manning Ave\nP.O. Box 336\nAlexander, ND 58831\nMonday-Friday: 8 a.m. - 4 p.m.\nSaturday-Sunday: Closed\nFacebook\nConnect\nFacebook\nWelcome to the City of Alexander, a small yet vibrant community rich in history and centrally located near Williston, Watford City and Sidney, MT. Established in 1905, Alexander has grown from a humble trading post to a charming town that offers a variety of local businesses, including cafes, repair shops and unique shopping experiences. With a strong sense of community, Alexander hosts annual events like Old Settler’s Days and is home to the Alexander Comets, whose school recently expanded its facilities. Whether you're visiting or considering making Alexander your home, we invite you to explore all we have to offer!\nQuick Links\nCity of Alexander: Utility Payments\nZoning District Map\nCity Boards and Councils\nCity of Alexander Contacts\nName | Position | | Phone | Contact | |\nKenneth Willcox |\nMayor of Alexander |\n|\n701-828-3461 |\nmayorofalexander@gmail.com |\n|\nHouston Engineering |\nCity Engineer |\n|\n|\n|\n|\nBrandi Gillespie |\nCity Auditor |\n|\n701-828-3461 |\ncityofalexander@ruggedwest.com |\n|\nHelpful\n-->\nShare\nFacebook\nTwitter\nEmail\n-->\nSize\n+\nReset\na\n−\nWelcome\nAbout\nCommunity\nNews\nEvents\nJobs\nEngage\nConnect\nFeedback\nHelp\nServices\nContact\nDirectory\nSitemap\nPowered by\n1 --> Get answers\nMy services\nMake a payment\nReport an issue\n1 -->\nSelect question type\nCorrectional Facility\nProperty and Housing\nBuilding Codes and Zoning\nJobs\nGeneral Government\nClose window\nSearch Site\nSearch\nClose window",
